Fix two misaligned-address constructs that GNAT rejects on 32-bit ARM

Langkit_Support is built with -gnatwe, and the bootstrap Liblktlang is always
built in dev mode, so any warning is fatal.  On targets that need strict
alignment (32-bit ARM) GNAT reports two real alignment problems:

* Generic_Bump_Ptr.Array_Alloc.Empty_Array_Access is a pointer to a "non-null
  junk address", and that address was 1:

    warning: source alignment (1) < alignment of "Element_Array" (4)

  for each of the dozens of instantiations in Liblktlang.  Use the alignment
  of Element_Array instead of 1: it is still a non-null address that is never
  dereferenced.

* Text.Decode overlaid a Text_Type (alignment 4) on the String returned by
  Iconv (alignment 1) with an Address clause:

    warning: specified address for "Text_Result" may be inconsistent with
    alignment / program execution may be erroneous (RM 13.3(27))

  Copy the bytes into the result instead.

The same two units are checked in under lkt/bootstrap/src (as Liblktlang_Support),
for the bootstrap build, and are changed the same way.

--- a/langkit/support/langkit_support-generic_bump_ptr.ads
+++ b/langkit/support/langkit_support-generic_bump_ptr.ads
@@ -113,10 +113,13 @@
         (Element_Array_Access, System.Address);
 
       Empty_Array_Access : constant Element_Array_Access := To_Pointer
-        (System.Null_Address + 1);
+        (System.Null_Address + Storage_Offset (Element_Array'Alignment));
       --  Access to an empty array. As accessing its elements is forbidden, but
       --  dereferencing it to take an empty slice is allowed, it is designed to
-      --  point to a non-null junk address.
+      --  point to a non-null junk address. That address is a multiple of the
+      --  alignment of Element_Array, as GNAT warns about converting an
+      --  address that cannot be aligned enough on targets that need strict
+      --  alignment (32-bit ARM, for instance).
 
       function Alloc
         (Pool : Bump_Ptr_Pool; Length : Natural) return Element_Array_Access
--- a/langkit/support/langkit_support-text.adb
+++ b/langkit/support/langkit_support-text.adb
@@ -158,10 +158,18 @@
          From_Code => Charset);
       pragma Assert (Result'Length mod 4 = 0);
 
-      Text_Result : constant Text_Type (1 .. Result'Length / 4)
-         with Import, Address => Result'Address;
    begin
-      return Text_Result;
+      --  Copy the bytes instead of overlaying a Text_Type on Result: the
+      --  alignment of Result is 1 while the one of Text_Type is 4, which GNAT
+      --  rightfully warns about on targets that need strict alignment.
+      return Text_Result : Text_Type (1 .. Result'Length / 4) do
+         declare
+            Bytes : String (1 .. Result'Length)
+               with Import, Address => Text_Result'Address;
+         begin
+            Bytes := Result;
+         end;
+      end return;
    end Decode;
 
    -------------
